<BaseLayout
  title="Julian Perez — Press & Media Coverage"
  description="Press coverage of Julian Perez: Resident Advisor, XLR8R, DJ Mag, Trommel Music, Vicious Magazine and more. Reviews, interviews and features."
>
  <main style="max-width:800px;margin:0 auto;padding:4rem 2rem;font-family:sans-serif;line-height:1.8;color:#111;">
    <nav style="margin-bottom:2rem;">
      <a href="/" style="color:#555;text-decoration:none;">← julianperez.com</a>
    </nav>

    <h1 style="font-size:2rem;margin-bottom:0.5rem;">Julian Perez — Press</h1>
    <p style="color:#555;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Media coverage, reviews and interviews.</p>

    <p style="margin-bottom:3rem;">Julian Perez has been featured in key electronic music publications including Resident Advisor, XLR8R, DJ Mag ES, Trommel Music, Vicious Magazine, Meoko, and Pulse Radio since 2009. Coverage spans album reviews, artist profiles, label features, festival appearances and interviews across Europe, Asia and the Americas. His debut album <em>Solemnity</em> (2016) and second album <em>Break-Even</em> (2021) received wide critical attention. His labels Fathers &amp; Sons Productions and Girada Unlimited have been covered as significant contributions to the underground vinyl scene.</p>

    <!-- QUOTES -->
    <h2 style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Selected Quotes</h2>

    <blockquote style="border-left:4px solid #111;padding-left:1.5rem;margin:0 0 1.5rem;color:#333;font-size:1.05rem;">
      "The way I see everything is changing. I feel like I'm on another level when I make music, when I DJ, it feels different. More confident."
      <footer style="font-size:0.85rem;color:#888;margin-top:0.5rem;">— Julian Perez · <a href="https://ra.co/news/26382" style="color:#888;">Resident Advisor, 2014</a></footer>
    </blockquote>

    <blockquote style="border-left:4px solid #111;padding-left:1.5rem;margin:0 0 1.5rem;color:#333;font-size:1.05rem;">
      "I think it's important for me as a DJ to always be playing different slots, and to be playing different shades of my sound, be it deeper or more big-room."
      <footer style="font-size:0.85rem;color:#888;margin-top:0.5rem;">— Julian Perez · <a href="https://ra.co/news/26382" style="color:#888;">Resident Advisor, 2014</a></footer>
    </blockquote>

    <blockquote style="border-left:4px solid #111;padding-left:1.5rem;margin:0 0 1.5rem;color:#333;font-size:1.05rem;">
      "You have to take care of yourself. I feel like self-discipline is a very important part of my job."
      <footer style="font-size:0.85rem;color:#888;margin-top:0.5rem;">— Julian Perez · <a href="https://ra.co/news/26382" style="color:#888;">Resident Advisor, 2014</a></footer>
    </blockquote>

    <blockquote style="border-left:4px solid #111;padding-left:1.5rem;margin:0 0 3rem;color:#333;font-size:1.05rem;">
      "A master of emotive, functional dance music, the distinct sound of Spanish wizard Julian Perez is heard in an instant."
      <footer style="font-size:0.85rem;color:#888;margin-top:0.5rem;">— Chris Nicholls · <a href="https://trommelmusic.com/music/premiere-a1-julian-perez-crack-a-joke-have-a-smoke-girada05/" style="color:#888;">Trommel Music, 2018</a></footer>
    </blockquote>

    <!-- FEATURED ARTICLES -->
    <h2 style="margin-bottom:2rem;">Featured Coverage</h2>

    <article style="margin-bottom:3rem;padding-bottom:3rem;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;">
      <p style="color:#888;font-size:0.85rem;margin-bottom:0.25rem;">Resident Advisor · September 12, 2014</p>
      <h3 style="font-size:1.2rem;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">
        <a href="https://ra.co/news/26382" style="color:#111;">RA Ibiza Weekly: Julian Perez, The Zoo Project</a>
      </h3>
      <p>Resident Advisor's Carlos Hawthorn profiled Julian Perez as one of 2014's breakthrough talents in Ibiza. The feature traced his journey from moving to the island in 2006 to establishing himself as a resident DJ and co-founder of Fathers &amp; Sons Productions. Perez spoke about his evolving artistic confidence, his philosophy of playing across different slots and sound shades, and the importance of self-discipline in his career. The article cemented his reputation as one of Ibiza's most consistent underground figures of the era.</p>
    </article>

    <article style="margin-bottom:3rem;padding-bottom:3rem;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;">
      <p style="color:#888;font-size:0.85rem;margin-bottom:0.25rem;">Resident Advisor · October 20, 2016</p>
      <h3 style="font-size:1.2rem;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">
        <a href="https://ra.co/news/36928" style="color:#111;">Julian Perez Releases Debut LP, Closes Fathers &amp; Sons Productions</a>
      </h3>
      <p>Resident Advisor covered the release of <em>Solemnity</em>, Julian Perez's debut album — a vinyl-only double LP and the final release on his imprint Fathers &amp; Sons Productions after twelve releases. The label had featured artists including S.A.M., Livio &amp; Roby, and Brian Harden. The 11-track album spans four sides of vinyl, demonstrating "Perez's attention to detail and the evolution of his groove-led style" — from atmospheric soundscapes and electro-influenced 909 drum patterns to deep dub techno. The title references "the state of being serious and dignified."</p>
      <p><strong>Tracklist:</strong> A1: Ain't That The Truth? / A2: Xless / A3: The Unspoken Thing / B1: Unusual Sense / B2: That Stuck TDK / B3: Interfluide / C1: Alog / C2: A War Melody Dreamer / D1: Sending Forth / D2: Recognition! / D3: Peace In The Darkness</p>
    </article>

    <article style="margin-bottom:3rem;padding-bottom:3rem;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;">
      <p style="color:#888;font-size:0.85rem;margin-bottom:0.25rem;">XLR8R · December 16, 2016</p>
      <h3 style="font-size:1.2rem;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">
        <a href="https://xlr8r.com/news/stream-snippets-of-julian-perezs-debut-album/" style="color:#111;">Stream Snippets of Julian Perez's Debut Album — Solemnity</a>
      </h3>
      <p>XLR8R covered the release of <em>Solemnity</em> as a showcase of "Perez's attention to detail and the evolution of his groove-led style." The album spans two 12-inch vinyl records with 11 tracks covering atmospheric soundscapes, electro-influenced 909 drum patterns, club-oriented compositions and deep dub techno influences. Available for pre-order through Subwax Bcn at the time of publication.</p>
    </article>

    <article style="margin-bottom:3rem;padding-bottom:3rem;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;">
      <p style="color:#888;font-size:0.85rem;margin-bottom:0.25rem;">Resident Advisor · March 18, 2016</p>
      <h3 style="font-size:1.2rem;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">
        <a href="https://ra.co/reviews/18750" style="color:#111;">Julian Perez – Now, After [Review]</a>
      </h3>
      <p>Resident Advisor reviewer Matt Unicomb reviewed Julian Perez's EP <em>Now, After</em> on Raum...musik (MUSIK096), describing it as versatile material for DJs managing the final stages of evening events. The title track features "bright keys and dubby synths" for an optimistic sonic palette, while B-side "Clue Me In" focuses on massive bass. The review noted that Perez had established himself through Fathers &amp; Sons Productions, producing sought-after vinyl that commands premium prices on the secondary market.</p>
    </article>

    <article style="margin-bottom:3rem;padding-bottom:3rem;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;">
      <p style="color:#888;font-size:0.85rem;margin-bottom:0.25rem;">Trommel Music · July 12, 2018</p>
      <h3 style="font-size:1.2rem;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">
        <a href="https://trommelmusic.com/featured/a-day-in-the-life-julian-perez" style="color:#111;">A Day In The Life: Julian Perez</a>
      </h3>
      <p>Alex Landzee followed Julian Perez during a weekend in Rotterdam, where he performed a 4-hour extended set at BAR Rotterdam (Void sound system). The feature described the Valencian-born producer as someone who carefully selects his engagements while maintaining active studio work and international bookings across Europe and North America. The article highlighted his two labels — Fathers and Sons and the newer Girada Unlimited, exploring experimental approaches within deep house and techno.</p>
    </article>

    <article style="margin-bottom:3rem;padding-bottom:3rem;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;">
      <p style="color:#888;font-size:0.85rem;margin-bottom:0.25rem;">XLR8R · November 6, 2018</p>
      <h3 style="font-size:1.2rem;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">
        <a href="https://xlr8r.com/news/premiere-hear-girada-unlimiteds-cure-music-debut/" style="color:#111;">Premiere: Hear Girada Unlimited's Cure Music Debut — A Ricardo Villalobos Favourite</a>
      </h3>
      <p>XLR8R premiered Girada Unlimited's seventh release on Cure Music. The A-side track "Zapatac" — a rework of Velodrome's 1988 composition "Capitaz" — became a favourite of Ricardo Villalobos, who included it in his BBC Radio 1 Essential Mix. The label drew inspiration from 1980s-90s Valencia club recordings and "La ruta del bakalao." Securing the rights took eight months and over 15 emails to reach the original artists.</p>
    </article>

    <article style="margin-bottom:3rem;padding-bottom:3rem;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;">
      <p style="color:#888;font-size:0.85rem;margin-bottom:0.25rem;">Trommel Music · October 3, 2018</p>
      <h3 style="font-size:1.2rem;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">
        <a href="https://trommelmusic.com/music/premiere-a1-julian-perez-crack-a-joke-have-a-smoke-girada05/" style="color:#111;">Premiere: A1 – Julian Perez – Crack a Joke, Have a Smoke [GIRADA05]</a>
      </h3>
      <p>Trommel Music's Chris Nicholls described Julian Perez as "a master of emotive, functional dance music" whose "distinct sound is heard in an instant." The fifth release on Girada Unlimited features three tracks — the A-side builds patiently over nine minutes with sharp acid sounds and layered melodies; B-sides include the after-hours "Mar De Fondo" and the energetic "Tense Capo."</p>
    </article>

    <article style="margin-bottom:3rem;padding-bottom:3rem;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;">
      <p style="color:#888;font-size:0.85rem;margin-bottom:0.25rem;">Trommel Music · February 14, 2019</p>
      <h3 style="font-size:1.2rem;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">
        <a href="https://trommelmusic.com/music/premiere-b1-julian-perez-and-franco-cinelli-beyond-1214-girada06/" style="color:#111;">Premiere: B1 – Julian Perez &amp; Franco Cinelli – Beyond 1214 [GIRADA06]</a>
      </h3>
      <p>Billy Wilkinson reviewed this collaborative EP between Julian Perez and Argentinian producer Franco Cinelli on Girada Unlimited. The title track "Beyond 1214" features "a haunting, spine-chilling bassline" with "choppy kick drums and electro-tinged snares," designed for peak-time moments. The B-side "Entre M Y 3" maintains "an incredibly eery, almost horror movie feel" through its "driving yet tormenting bassline."</p>
    </article>

    <article style="margin-bottom:3rem;padding-bottom:3rem;border-bottom:1px solid #eee;">
      <p style="color:#888;font-size:0.85rem;margin-bottom:0.25rem;">Trommel Music · May 17, 2021</p>
      <h3 style="font-size:1.2rem;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">
        <a href="https://trommelmusic.com/music/reviews/review-julian-perez-break-even-lp-girada010/" style="color:#111;">Review: Julian Perez – Break-Even LP [GIRADA010]</a>
      </h3>
      <p>Trommel Music reviewed <em>Break-Even</em>, the landmark tenth release on Girada Unlimited — a double 12" vinyl spanning spacey breakbeats, lush atmospherics and deep house across four sides. "Energy Fever" was highlighted as "a sublime piece of dream house more than capable of entrancing a dancefloor" and "CSO All The Way" as "a shimmering piece of cosmic breaks." Tracks include Sweentro, Facts, Revelation, Eveileb and Drowned In Faith (Love &amp; Light).</p>
    </article>

